<title>USA: Massachusetts Senate passes $18.3 bln budget.</title>
<headline>Massachusetts Senate passes $18.3 bln budget.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Massachusetts State Senate, after two days of debate, passed an $18.3 billion budget late Wednesday night.</p>
<p>The measure, which includes a move to retire $134 million of fiscal recovery bonds before the end of June, now heads to a conference committee made up of six members -- three from the House and three from the Senate -- who are expected to be named early next week.</p>
<p>((--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106))</p>
